WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.133
[music]

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.733
[Instructor] Now we can control
the enemies spawning

3
00:00:08.733 --> 00:00:11.133
whenever they all leave the scene.

4
00:00:11.933 --> 00:00:13.800
So what we're going to do is

5
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.866
increase the number of enemies
every time we defeat a wave.

6
00:00:17.366 --> 00:00:21.433
So, we'll have 1 spawn, and then we can
have 2 spawn, and 3, and so on.

7
00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:25.266
In our SpawnManager Script

8
00:00:25.366 --> 00:00:28.600
we're going to use
a variable to control...

9
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.100
the actual number
of enemies in the wave.

10
00:00:32.433 --> 00:00:35.866
So, we'll make a public variable
so we can see what it does again,

11
00:00:36.666 --> 00:00:38.700
make it an Integer,

12
00:00:38.933 --> 00:00:41.600
and then we'll call it "waveNumber,"

13
00:00:43.366 --> 00:00:45.700
and we'll set it to 1
in the beginning,

14
00:00:46.266 --> 00:00:49.666
and then we'll actually use
this waveNumber to dictate

15
00:00:49.666 --> 00:00:51.666
how many enemies should spawn

16
00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:53.633
after we defeat every enemy.

17
00:00:53.633 --> 00:00:56.200
In our "if() statement," 
since this is where we know

18
00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.100
when enemies are defeated,

19
00:00:58.533 --> 00:01:01.333
this is actually where we'll "increment"
our waveNumber.

20
00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:05.100
So we'll change
our "SpawnEnemyWave(),"

21
00:01:05.766 --> 00:01:07.766
and start to be wave number,

22
00:01:08.766 --> 00:01:11.266
so this will spawn 1
enemy at the beginning.

23
00:01:12.233 --> 00:01:14.533
Now, when we've defeated
all of the enemies

24
00:01:14.533 --> 00:01:16.466
we'll set waveNumber,

25
00:01:16.466 --> 00:01:19.733
and we'll use
that "++," this time.

26
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.700
So now when the enemies
are all defeated,

27
00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:25.066
it will increase waveNumber by 1,

28
00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.200
so now waveNumber should be 2.

29
00:01:27.266 --> 00:01:29.500
And then if we change the enemies

30
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.266
to Spawn Parameter,
to be a wave number here,

31
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.800
so then it should spawn
2 enemies afterwards.

32
00:01:36.733 --> 00:01:38.566
So, now if we test
our game,

33
00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:42.200
we should see 1 enemy spawn;
there we go.

34
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.566
And then if we hit
this enemy off,

35
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:48.133
2 enemies spawn.
Then see if we can hit both.

36
00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:50.133
Oh, we have 1.

37
00:01:51.733 --> 00:01:54.200
And the last 1
will go off,

38
00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.700
and then do we get 3?

39
00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:58.800
And there you go.

40
00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.400
So, now in your SpawnManager Script,

41
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.466
you're going to add
another variable

42
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.333
to keep track of the waveNumber.

43
00:02:08.633 --> 00:02:10.500
So we'll set it to 1,
and we'll make it public

44
00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.566
so we can see what it's doing.

45
00:02:12.766 --> 00:02:16.800
In our Start() Method,
change EnemyWave to waveNumber,

46
00:02:18.966 --> 00:02:21.533
and then in our Update() Method,
where we can actually keep track

47
00:02:21.533 --> 00:02:24.133
of when we hit the point
where all the enemies

48
00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:26.566
are off the scene,
and we create a new one,

49
00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:29.133
we'll increment wave number
by 1 here,

50
00:02:29.666 --> 00:02:32.933
and then we'll spawn 
a new EnemyWave using

51
00:02:32.933 --> 00:02:34.933
the incremented number.

52
00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:37.333
Now it's your turn.

53
00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.100
